# City Prompt — District Kits Research

## What Are District Kits?

A "District Kit" is a curated set of building, street, and park archetypes that go together to create a cohesive neighbourhood character. Instead of mixing random styles, users pick a kit and get everything they need to build a convincing district.

## Current State (163 archetypes)

- **96 buildings** across 60 categories — most have only 1-2 archetypes per style
- **26 streets** — good variety but not style-matched to building kits
- **41 parks/plazas** — well distributed but generic (not style-specific)

The biggest gap: most building categories have only 1-2 types. You can't build a cohesive Parisian district with just 2 building archetypes. A full kit needs 6-10 building types + matching streets + matching parks.

